A||N||6||Heisenhund||Can you describe the ruckus?||||5||
Z||000000||Heisenhund||01-01-2001||06:29 AM||||My 85 GT has a noise. It can best be described as a whine that starts at about 35 MPH, gets the loudest at about 40 MPH, then goes away by 50 MPH. The car is an auto so I checked the fluid first. Added about ½ pint to bring it to full. Still whines. It's definitely MPH related, not RPM.<P>Any ideas anyone?<P>Thanks,<BR>Heis<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||ka4nkf||01-01-2001||11:47 AM||||My 86 does that too. it seems that it only does it when i first start up in the morning and goes away after i drive a awhile.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||01-01-2001||04:38 PM||||My car had the same kind for noise that was MPH related. The funny thing was that the noise also altered its pitch if I turned (like on a curve in the road or just put a little weight on one side during a lane change.) It was like a moaning banshee when it would get really loud and it was coming from the back.<P>The problem?<P>A rear wheel bearing was worn out. You could move the wheel slightly because the bearing had worn out the tolerances. Easy fix when you take off the caliper and rotor! <P>Hope this helps!||||reg||6
Z||000003||Heisenhund||01-01-2001||05:11 PM||||OK, that's what I'm thinking too. I'll have to pay closer attention to the ruckus when turning. Maybe replace the bearings anyway once my 86 GT gets back on the ground<P>Thanka again,<BR>Heis<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||01-02-2001||05:14 AM||||Wheel bearing or CV joint, I'd guess.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||01-02-2001||11:50 AM||||Just for grins, try rotating your tires front to back. See if the noise goes away or moves. If the rear end is out of alignment, it can cause the tires to wear unevenly. Will make it sound like a truck tire.<BR>Having said all of that... it's still probably going to be the bearing.<BR>Have experienced both situations, but the first fix is free.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Heisenhund||01-02-2001||12:07 PM||||Excellent suggestion! I was trying to think of something that could eliminate a couple other possibilities. I've had the same rear end problem on another car & noticed a very similar noise. Hadn't thought of rotating the tires yet though. Good plan! And cheap!<P>Heis<BR>||||reg||14
